# cdsi-engine targets Java 8

`cdsi-engine` compiles with `<release>8</release>` because other Java 8 projects use it
as a dependency. The rest of the repository (`cdsi-web`, `cdsi-fits-tests`) is Java 17,
so code that is fine there is not fine here.

Do not use, in `cdsi-engine/src/**`:
- `var`, records, sealed classes, switch expressions / arrow cases, text blocks,
  pattern-matching `instanceof`
- `List.of` / `Set.of` / `Map.of` / `copyOf`, `Stream.toList()`, `Collectors.toUnmodifiable*`
- `Optional.isEmpty()` / `orElseThrow()` (no-arg) / `ifPresentOrElse` / `stream()`
- `String.isBlank()` / `strip()` / `repeat()` / `lines()`, `@Deprecated(since=..., forRemoval=...)`

The build fails on these. Write the Java 8 equivalent (`Arrays.asList`,
`Collections.unmodifiableList`, `collect(Collectors.toList())`, `trim().isEmpty()`, ...).
Never raise the engine's `<release>` to make code compile.
